  "input": "あなたは英語学習コンテンツの独立評価者です。以下の英語記事から「英語上級者が学ぶ価値のあるKey Phrase」を選ぶ課題があり、\n複数の匿名の選定結果(セット S1〜Sn、各5件以内)があります。各候補を下記rubricで採点してください。どのセットがどのモデルの結果かは不明です。\n\n【選定時に参加者へ与えられた条件(参考)】\n1. 本文中の連続した語句だけを抜き出す(一般化以外の変更・言い換え・追加・創作は禁止)。\n2. 一般化後5語以内。\n3. 固有名詞や特定の人物・物事を指す部分は、意味と文法を保って ~ / A / B / someone / something 等に置き換える(一般化できる場合は必ず行う)。\n4. 上級者でも学ぶ価値のある語彙・イディオム・慣用表現を優先する。\n5. 基本語だけで構成され字面どおりに意味が分かる表現や、上級者なら知っている易しい表現は除外する。\n6. 条件を満たす候補から5件選ぶ。適切な候補が不足する場合のみ5件未満とし、数合わせはしない。\n\n【採点rubric(各候補、各0〜2の整数)】\n- G 一般化の適切さ: 2=本文固有の固有名詞・特定の人物/物事が適切に一般化されている、または一般化すべき要素がなく原文のままで適切 / 1=一般化が不十分または過剰、あるいは軽微な不自然さ / 0=一般化すべき固有要素が残って学習価値を損なう、または一般化で意味・文法が壊れている。\n- V 上級者向け学習価値: 2=上級者でも学ぶ価値が明確(句動詞・イディオム・コロケーション・語法・語彙として) / 1=価値はあるが中程度、または一部平易 / 0=学習価値がほぼない。\n- E 易しさの排除: 2=易しい表現ではない(意味が字面から自明でない) / 1=やや易しいが慣用的な意味や語法の学びはある / 0=基本語のみで字面どおり、上級者なら当然知っている。\n- N 単位の自然さ: 2=自然で完結した学習単位 / 1=余分な語または不足があるが許容 / 0=中途半端に切られている・不自然。\n- needs_generalization: その候補の元の表現に、一般化(~, A/B, someone, something等)すべき要素が本文上あったか(true/false)。\nセット単位: padding = 5件を埋めるために学習価値の低い候補(V<=0またはE<=0)を入れていると判断するか(true/false)。\n\n【注意】\n- 本文との一致・語数は別途機械検証するため、ここでは採点対象外。ただし本文に明らかに存在しない表現と気付いた場合のみ noteに \"not_in_text\" と書く。\n- 候補の優劣を、セットの並び順やセットIDから推測しない。各候補を独立に採点する。\n- 候補が0件のセットは candidates を空配列にする。\n\n【出力】JSONのみ(説明文・コードフェンス不要)。noteは通常は空文字、本文に存在しない表現と気付いた場合のみ \"not_in_text\"。形式:\n{\"sets\":[{\"set_id\":\"S1\",\"padding\":false,\"candidates\":[{\"idx\":1,\"G\":2,\"V\":2,\"E\":1,\"N\":2,\"needs_generalization\":false,\"note\":\"\"}]}]}\n\n\n【記事】\n\n# 20% Plan Taken Back—but the Oil Chart Was Not Done Yet\n\nThis news feels like a short play in three acts. Act One was “20%.” Act Two brought a surprise. Act Three was an unexpected move in oil prices.\n\nThe curtain rose on July 13. At 10:16 a.m., Trump posted about a US plan. The United States would seek a 20% charge on all cargo passing through the Strait of Hormuz. The aim was to recover the cost of US efforts to keep the strait safe.\n\nBut “20%” was not a finished system. The post did not say who would pay. It did not say how the money would be collected. It did not say what law would support it. For the moment, only a large number stood at center stage.\n\nThe number stayed at center stage for about a day. Then the story took a sharp turn.\n\n### The 20% plan changes overnight\n\nAbout 24 hours and 48 minutes later, at 11:04 a.m. on July 14, Trump made another post. He said the 20% plan would be replaced by trade and investment projects between Gulf states and the US. He cited “very productive discussions” with Middle Eastern leaders. He also said no one should charge ships in the Strait. He said he disliked fees.\n\nThe change was sudden. But the dates must stay separate to understand the oil move. On July 13, Brent rose 9.59% and settled at $83.30. Reuters linked that rise to concern about a US sea blockade of Iran. The blockade was planned for the next day. Reuters also linked it to energy shipments through the Strait of Hormuz.\n\n### The chart refuses to stay down\n\nAfter the withdrawal and replacement announcement, Brent crude futures briefly gave back some gains. Soon, they returned close to the high level before the announcement. At the time of reporting, Brent was up about 2.6%, above $85 a barrel. Its final settlement price was $84.73, up 1.7% from the day before.\n\n## In one line\n\nConcerns about US-Iran attacks, the sea blockade, and tanker safety continued on July 14. So the flashy 20% plan left the stage. But the chart pulled back only briefly before recovering. The policy turn and the oil chart’s “not over yet” move happened that same day.\n\n\n【匿名の選定結果】\n\nS1:\n  1. short play in three acts\n  2. stayed at center stage\n  3. took a sharp turn\n  4. gave back some gains\n  5. settled at ~\n\nS2:\n  1. take a sharp turn\n  2. cite ~\n  3. sea blockade of ~\n  4. give back some gains\n  5. pull back\n\nS3:\n  1. gave back some gains\n  2. pulled back only briefly\n  3. settled at ~\n  4. took a sharp turn\n  5. recover the cost of\n\nS4:\n  1. blockade\n  2. crude futures\n  3. gave back some gains\n  4. settlement price\n  5. pulled back\n\nS5:\n  1. took a sharp turn\n  2. stood at center stage\n  3. gave back some gains\n  4. The curtain rose on ~\n  5. settled at ~\n\nS6:\n  1. give back gains\n  2. sea blockade\n  3. Brent crude futures\n  4. take a sharp turn\n  5. settle at\n\nS7:\n  1. recover the cost of\n  2. took a sharp turn\n  3. linked that rise to concern\n  4. gave back some gains\n  5. final settlement price\n",
